  abstract = {{Developing software product lines involves modeling a large number of features, usually using feature models, that represent different viewpoints, sub-systems or concerns of the software system.
To manage complexity on a large scale, there is a need to separate, relate and compose
several feature models while automating the reasoning on their
compositions.
This demonstration gives an overview of a Domain-Specific Language, FAMILIAR, that is dedicated
to the management of feature models.
Its comprehensive programming environment, based on Eclipse, is also described. It complements existing tool support (i.e., FeatureIDE).}}
}

